 		Reading returns 1 if boost is active, 0 otherwise.
-		Writing 1 or 0 toggles bit 4 of EC status register 0x07A5.
+		Writing 1 or 0 toggles bit 6 of EC performance register 0x0751.
+
+What:		/sys/devices/platform/tuxedo_keyboard/over_boost
+Date:		September 2026
+KernelVersion:	6.1
+Contact:	OpenMechrevo Authors <dev@openmechrevo.org>
+Description:
+		OverBoost indicator status via EC 0x07A5 bit 4 (0x10).
+		Reading returns 1 if overboost is active, 0 otherwise.
 
 What:		/sys/devices/platform/tuxedo_keyboard/dgpu_power
 Date:		September 2026
 KernelVersion:	6.1
 Contact:	OpenMechrevo Authors <dev@openmechrevo.org>
 Description:
-		[UNVERIFIED: REBOOT PREFERRED]: Discrete GPU PCIe slot power control.
+		Discrete GPU PCIe slot power status (READ-ONLY).
 		Reading calls ACPI AMW0.OEMG(0x0300, 2) and returns 1 if powered
-		(0xAA) or 0 if cut (0x55).
-		Writing 0 invokes OEMG(0x0300, 1) cutting PCIe slot power; writing 1
-		invokes OEMG(0x0300, 0) restoring power.
-		WARNING: Userspace MUST unbind GPU kernel driver and remove the PCIe
-		device before writing 0. On GM5HG0A platforms, switching graphics
-		modes is designed to take effect after system reboot (via MUX NVRAM).
+		(0xAA) or 0 if cut (0x55). Dynamic power cut at runtime is disabled
+		to prevent PCIe Surprise Down AER kernel panic. Display switching
+		requires reboot via MUX NVRAM.
 
 What:		/sys/devices/platform/tuxedo_keyboard/mux_scheme
 Date:		September 2026
